# Integer32 addition promotes overflow to int64

Adds 1 to the int32 maximum to verify the result promotes to int64 instead
of failing, then adds 1 again to verify chained arithmetic keeps using the
promoted representation. Both declarations keep the static int32 type while
the runtime values use the wider precision.

>>> source
maximum: int32 = 2147483647
unit: int32 = 1

overflow: int32 = maximum + unit
print(overflow)

chained: int32 = overflow + unit
print(chained)

<<< stdout
2147483648
2147483649

<<< stderr
